#: src/ai/text-threads.md:3
msgid "Text Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:5
msgid ""
"Text threads in the [Agent Panel](./agent-panel.md) work like a regular "
"editor. You can use custom keybindings, multiple cursors, and all the "
"standard editing features while chatting."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:8
msgid "Text Threads vs. Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:10
msgid ""
"Text Threads were Zed's original AI interface. In May 2025, Zed introduced "
"the current [Agent Panel](./agent-panel.md), designed for agentic workflows."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:13
msgid ""
"The key difference: text threads don't support tool calls and many other "
"more modern agentic features. They can't autonomously read files, write "
"code, or run commands on your behalf. Text Threads are for simpler "
"conversational interactions where you send text and receive text responses "
"back."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:17
msgid ""
"Therefore, [MCP servers](./mcp.md) and [external agents](./external-agents."
"md) are also not available in Text Threads."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:19
msgid "Usage Overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:21
msgid "Text threads organize content into message blocks with roles:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:23
msgid "`You`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:24
msgid "`Assistant`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:25
msgid "`System`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:27
msgid ""
"To begin, type your message in a `You` block. As you type, the remaining "
"token count for the selected model updates automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:30
msgid ""
"To add context from an editor, highlight text and run `agent: add selection "
"to thread` (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd->|ctrl-></kbd>). If the selection "
"is code, Zed will wrap it in a fenced code block."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:33
msgid ""
"To submit a message, use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-enter|ctrl-enter</"
"kbd> (`assistant: assist`). In text threads, <kbd class=\"keybinding\">enter|"
"enter</kbd> inserts a new line instead of submitting, which preserves "
"standard editor behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:36
msgid ""
"After you submit a message, the response is streamed below in an `Assistant` "
"message block. You can cancel the stream at any point with <kbd>escape</"
"kbd>, or start a new conversation at any time via <kbd>cmd-n|ctrl-n</kbd>."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:39
msgid ""
"Text threads support straightforward conversations, but you can also go back "
"and edit earlier messages—including previous LLM responses—to change "
"direction, refine context, or correct mistakes without starting a new thread "
"or spending tokens on follow-up corrections. If you want to remove a message "
"block entirely, place your cursor at the beginning of the block and use the "
"`delete` key."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:42
msgid ""
"A typical workflow might involve making edits and adjustments throughout the "
"context to refine your inquiry or provide additional information. Here's an "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:45
msgid "Write text in a `You` block."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:46 src/ai/text-threads.md:51
msgid ""
"Submit the message with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-enter|ctrl-enter</kbd>."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:47
msgid "Receive an `Assistant` response that doesn't meet your expectations."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:48
msgid "Cancel the response with <kbd>escape</kbd>."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:49
msgid ""
"Erase the content of the `Assistant` message block and remove the block "
"entirely."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:50
msgid "Add additional context to your original message."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:53
msgid ""
"You can also cycle the role of a message block by clicking on the role, "
"which is useful when you receive a response in an `Assistant` block that you "
"want to edit and send back up as a `You` block."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:55
msgid "Commands Overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:57
msgid "Type `/` at the beginning of a line to see available slash commands:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:59
msgid "`/default`: Inserts the default rule"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:60
msgid ""
"`/diagnostics`: Injects errors reported by the project's language server"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:61
msgid "`/fetch`: Fetches the content of a webpage and inserts it"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:62
msgid "`/file`: Inserts a single file or a directory of files"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:63
msgid "`/now`: Inserts the current date and time"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:64
msgid ""
"`/prompt`: Adds a custom-configured prompt to the context ([see Rules "
"Library](./rules.md#rules-library))"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:65
msgid "`/symbols`: Inserts the current tab's active symbols"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:66
msgid "`/tab`: Inserts the content of the active tab or all open tabs"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:67
msgid ""
"`/terminal`: Inserts a select number of lines of output from the terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:68
msgid "`/selection`: Inserts the selected text"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:70
msgid ""
"**Note:** Remember, commands are only evaluated when the text thread is "
"created or when the command is inserted, so a command like `/now` won't "
"continuously update, or `/file` commands won't keep their contents up to "
"date."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:72
msgid "`/default`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:74
msgid ""
"Read more about `/default` in the [Rules: Editing the Default Rules](./rules."
"md#default-rules) section."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:76
msgid "Usage: `/default`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:78
msgid "`/diagnostics`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:80
msgid ""
"Injects errors reported by the project's language server into the context."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:82
msgid "Usage: `/diagnostics [--include-warnings] [path]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:84
msgid ""
"`--include-warnings`: Optional flag to include warnings in addition to "
"errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:85
msgid ""
"`path`: Optional path to limit diagnostics to a specific file or directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:87
msgid "`/file`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:89
msgid ""
"Inserts the content of a file or directory into the context. Supports glob "
"patterns."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:91
msgid "Usage: `/file <path>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:93 src/ai/text-threads.md:128
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr "範例："

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:95
msgid ""
"`/file src/index.js` - Inserts the content of `src/index.js` into the "
"context."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:96
msgid ""
"`/file src/*.js` - Inserts the content of all `.js` files in the `src` "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:97
msgid "`/file src` - Inserts the content of all files in the `src` directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:99
msgid "`/now`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:101
msgid ""
"Inserts the current date and time. Useful for informing the model about its "
"knowledge cutoff relative to now."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:103
msgid "Usage: `/now`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:105
msgid "`/prompt`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:107
msgid ""
"Inserts a rule from the Rules Library into the context. Rules can nest other "
"rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:109
msgid "Usage: `/prompt <prompt_name>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:111
msgid "Related: `/default`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:113
msgid "`/symbols`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:115
msgid ""
"Inserts the active symbols (functions, classes, etc.) from the current tab, "
"providing a structural overview of the file."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:117
msgid "Usage: `/symbols`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:119
msgid "`/tab`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:121
msgid "Inserts the content of the active tab or all open tabs."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:123
msgid "Usage: `/tab [tab_name|all]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:125
msgid "`tab_name`: Optional name of a specific tab to insert."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:126
msgid "`all`: Insert content from all open tabs."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:130
msgid "`/tab` - Inserts the content of the active tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:131
msgid ""
"`/tab \"index.js\"` - Inserts the content of the tab named \"index.js\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:132
msgid "`/tab all` - Inserts the content of all open tabs."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:134
msgid "`/terminal`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:136
msgid "Inserts recent terminal output (default: 50 lines)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:138
msgid "Usage: `/terminal [<number>]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:140
msgid ""
"`<number>`: Optional parameter to specify the number of lines to insert "
"(default is 50)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:142
msgid "`/selection`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:144
msgid ""
"Inserts the currently selected text. Equivalent to `agent: add selection to "
"thread` (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd->|ctrl-></kbd>)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:146
msgid "Usage: `/selection`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:148
msgid "Commands in the Rules Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:150
msgid ""
"[Commands](#commands) can be used in rules, in the Rules Library (previously "
"known as Prompt Library), to insert dynamic content or perform actions. For "
"example, if you want to create a rule where it is important for the model to "
"know the date, you can use the `/now` command to insert the current date."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:155
msgid ""
"Slash commands in rules **only** work when they are used in text threads. "
"Using them in non-text threads is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:159
msgid "**Note:** Slash commands in rules **must** be on their own line."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:161
msgid ""
"See the [list of commands](#commands) above for more information on "
"commands, and what slash commands are available."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:163 src/ai/text-threads.md:185
msgid "Example"
msgstr "範例"

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:173
msgid ""
"In the above example, the `/file` command is used to insert the contents of "
"the `Cargo.toml` file (or all `Cargo.toml` files present in the project) "
"into the rule."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:175
msgid "Nesting Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:177
msgid ""
"Similar to adding rules to the default rules, you can nest rules within "
"other rules with the `/prompt` command (only supported in Text Threads "
"currently)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:179
msgid "You might want to nest rules to:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:181
msgid "Create templates on the fly"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:182
msgid ""
"Break collections like docs or references into smaller, mix-and-matchable "
"parts"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:183
msgid ""
"Create variants of a similar rule (e.g., `Async Rust - Tokio` vs. `Async "
"Rust - Async-std`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:201
msgid ""
"_The text in parentheses above are comments and are not part of the rule._"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:203
msgid ""
"**Note:** You can technically nest a rule within itself, but we don't "
"recommend doing so."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:205
msgid ""
"By using nested rules, you can create modular and reusable rule components "
"that can be combined in various ways to suit different scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:207
msgid ""
"**Note:** When using slash commands to bring in additional context, the "
"injected content can be edited directly inline in the text thread—edits here "
"will not propagate to the saved rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:209
msgid "Extensibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:211
msgid "Additional slash commands can be provided by extensions."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:213
msgid ""
"See [Extension: Slash Commands](../extensions/slash-commands.md) to learn "
"how to create your own."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:215
msgid "Advanced Concepts"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:217
msgid "Rule Templates"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:219
msgid ""
"Zed uses rule templates to power internal assistant features, like the "
"terminal assistant, or the content rules used in the inline assistant."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:221
msgid "Zed has the following internal rule templates:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:223
msgid "`content_prompt.hbs`: Used for generating content in the editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:224
msgid ""
"`terminal_assistant_prompt.hbs`: Used for the terminal assistant feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:226
msgid ""
"At this point it is unknown if we will expand templates further to be user-"
"creatable."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:228
msgid "Overriding Templates"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:230
msgid ""
"**Note:** It is not recommended to override templates unless you know what "
"you are doing. Editing templates will break your assistant if done "
"incorrectly."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:232
msgid ""
"Zed allows you to override the default rules used for various assistant "
"features by placing custom Handlebars (.hbs) templates in your `~/.config/"
"zed/prompt_overrides` directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:234
msgid "The following templates can be overridden:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:236
msgid ""
"[`content_prompt.hbs`](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/tree/main/"
"assets/prompts/content_prompt.hbs): Used for generating content in the "
"editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:238
msgid ""
"[`terminal_assistant_prompt.hbs`](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/tree/"
"main/assets/prompts/terminal_assistant_prompt.hbs): Used for the terminal "
"assistant feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:240
msgid ""
"**Note:** Be sure you want to override these, as you'll miss out on "
"iteration on our built-in features. This should be primarily used when "
"developing Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:243
msgid ""
"You can customize these templates to better suit your needs while "
"maintaining the core structure and variables used by Zed. Zed will "
"automatically reload your prompt overrides when they change on disk."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:246
msgid ""
"Consult Zed's [assets/prompts](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/tree/"
"main/assets/prompts) directory for current versions you can play with."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:248
msgid "History"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:250
msgid ""
"After you submit your first message in a text thread, a name for your "
"context is generated by the language model, and the context is automatically "
"saved to your file system in"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:252
msgid "`~/.config/zed/conversations` (macOS)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:253
msgid "`~/.local/share/zed/conversations` (Linux)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:254
msgid "`%LocalAppData%\\Zed\\conversations` (Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:256
msgid ""
"You can access and load previous contexts by clicking on the history button "
"in the top-left corner of the agent panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/text-threads.md:258
msgid ""
"![Viewing assistant history](https://zed.dev/img/assistant/assistant-history."
"png)"
msgstr ""

